{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "02YL", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-descending-properties-morphisms-fppf}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:42a5a9ed84a8a0a03722c569d24b575109dd63f3229a16e9298b78037de36424", "source_text": "Properties of morphisms local in the fppf topology on the target", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3ecbaacb7c4aacfa38429583bc6b792a26a8f77af78d90c88a717d02c41d8e6a", "unit_id": "tag:02YL:title"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02YL", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:869e14a86237711c4c898a9ec753d26dd8111fc9621f62bb456aa2d791ad3029", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we find some properties of morphisms of schemes\nfor which we could not (yet) show they are local on the base in\nthe fpqc topology which, however, are local on the base\nin the fppf topology.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b23fd95c9d63193a0ef2beaf31f30cab774f52c207960e6ddaebc9f75ca6b790", "unit_id": "tag:02YL:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-fppf-property-immersion}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:46ff78bd34b23aa53b324b884c37649a627b0593998ca6dc0fe9b27a4196f15d", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is an immersion''\nis fppf local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fc765921238b00834e3209fe7f8bc64e0237c979e1fb2f4057f5b3b95b180bd2", "unit_id": "tag:02YM:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\pi : S' \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\pi : S' \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$f' : X' \\to S'$", "MATH_0005": "$f'(X') = \\pi^{-1}(f(X))$", "MATH_0006": "$f(X) \\subset S$", "MATH_0007": "$Z \\subset S$", "MATH_0008": "$Z = \\overline{f(X)} \\setminus f(X)$", "MATH_0009": "$f'(X')$", "MATH_0010": "$S' \\setminus Z'$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{S' \\setminus Z' \\to S \\setminus Z\\}$", "MATH_0012": "$f : X \\to S \\setminus Z$", "MATH_0013": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-base-change-immersion}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-fppf-open}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{topology-lemma-open-morphism-quotient-topology}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{topology-lemma-open-morphism-quotient-topology}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-closed-immersion}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties-morphisms}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:da604bf1ca77b01f68af50c4880b95c6f1d89cab689d8e6d65e96760a9040eaf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:adb797e302d7fc60afc836e053bcfce2f8c2e2f694860dea62d3fd13a0a81c52", "source_text": "The property of being an immersion is stable under base change,\nsee Schemes, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThe property of being an immersion is Zariski local on the base.\nFinally, let\n<MATH_0001> be a surjective morphism of affine schemes,\nwhich is flat and locally of finite presentation.\nNote that <MATH_0002> is open by\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a morphism.\nAssume that the base change <MATH_0004> is an immersion.\nIn particular we see that <MATH_0005> is locally closed.\nHence by Topology, Lemma <REF_0003>\nwe see that <MATH_0006>\nis locally closed. Let <MATH_0007> be\nthe closed subset <MATH_0008>.\nBy Topology, Lemma <REF_0004>\nagain we see that <MATH_0009> is closed in <MATH_0010>.\nHence we may apply Lemma <REF_0005>\nto the fpqc covering <MATH_0011>\nand conclude that <MATH_0012> is a closed\nimmersion. In other words, <MATH_0013> is an immersion.\nTherefore Lemma <REF_0006> applies and we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d29b88e2c0d5c3988ea78404658f212b877472a8b848338778d3ca0b40760644", "unit_id": "tag:02YM:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-fppf-property-dominant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f8700c5e06e1c5e30d596cb75e974686e1b4517dd1407734765a7d79dd68382e", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is dominant''\nis fppf local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1b9cf379e302f96c2e8005e1785836a7a433923c9534877700fd80430bb22986", "unit_id": "tag:0H8J:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f' : X' \\to S'$", "MATH_0004": "$X' \\to S'\\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$X' \\to X \\to S$", "MATH_0006": "$X\\to S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-open-base-change-dominant}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-fppf-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f3772391b85f36bf170ab81d5dd36a4da08e13a28c779ad31cc8006439a37cb7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b4ae56085802b9dad77f55eb1ddb02107bc6cfd31c20c3414c6e2dffc73fa1c6", "source_text": "By Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>,\ndominant morphisms are preserved\nunder pullback by open morphisms, hence\nby flat morphisms locally of finite presentation\n(Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0002>).\nThe other direction is easier.\nIndeed, being dominant is clearly Zariski local on the base.\nNext, let <MATH_0001> be a surjective morphism of schemes\n(not necessarily flat or locally of finite\npresentation),\nand let <MATH_0002> be a morphism. Assume that the base change\n<MATH_0003> is dominant. Then <MATH_0004> is a composition\nof two dominant morphisms, hence dominant. Since this is also\nthe composition <MATH_0005>, it follows that <MATH_0006> is dominant.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:32020c1b89b5e2c426e5dd1e6055123e53cd9dcb90a68579c32e640519cf9294", "unit_id": "tag:0H8J:proof"}
